course: dictionary
lesson: 13428
title: Homecoming and two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Homecoming is a noun made from two words, home and coming. Put them together and you get coming home, which is its first meaning: coming home after being away for a long time. «After three years at sea, Dad's homecoming was the best day of our lives.»
explain: Soldiers, sailors and travellers often have a homecoming. So do you, when you come back from a long holiday. The word is warm and emotional, because it is about being welcomed back.
explain: In the USA and Canada, homecoming also means a yearly party at a school or college. It usually has a football game and a dance, and former pupils are welcomed back. «The homecoming dance is on Friday night.»
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. If the sentence talks about a long time away, it is the first meaning. If it talks about a football game or a dance, it is the second.
fact: Homecoming means coming home after being away for a long time.
fact: In the USA and Canada, homecoming is a yearly celebration at a school or college.
fact: A school homecoming usually has a football game and a dance, and former pupils are welcomed back.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the chapter «Dulce Domum» tells of Mole's homecoming to Mole End at Christmas.
exercise: «After three years at sea, Dad's homecoming was the best day of our lives.» What does homecoming mean here? | A party at school with a football game | A big meal in the garden | *Coming home after being away for a long time | A trip to the seaside
exercise: «The homecoming dance is on Friday, and past pupils are coming back.» What is the homecoming in this sentence? | A day when the school closes | *A yearly school celebration with a football game and a dance | A long journey by sea | A test that everyone must sit on Friday
exercise: «The soldiers' homecoming was full of flags and hugs.» Find and copy the word that names the event of coming home. | soldiers | flags | hugs | *homecoming
test: «Mole's homecoming to Mole End was warm and happy.» What does homecoming mean in this sentence? | A football game at school | *Coming home after a long time away | A meal shared with friends | A yearly dance for former pupils
test: Which sentence uses homecoming to mean a school event? | *«The homecoming game starts at six, and the dance follows.» | «Her homecoming was full of tears and hugs.» | «The homecoming took three years, across the sea.» | «The homecoming bags were packed for the trip.»
exam: Mia says a homecoming is always a party with a football game. Is she right? | Yes, but only in Scotland | *No, it can also mean coming home after being away for a long time | No, it is a kind of food | Yes, a homecoming is always a school party
